~ _chapter4_echo
Preserved Citizen: You kept us safe in the Null Court. The mirrors call it kindness. Some of us call it a softer lock.
Kaelen: If safety feels like captivity, I need to hear that before I call it mercy.
Released Citizen: You opened the door. We ran. Some of us found sky. Some of us found that our homes had no place left to load.
Kaelen: Freedom without preparation can still hurt people. I have to carry that too.
Contracted Citizen: Your bargain gave us a path out. It also taught SOVEREIGN exactly which words make you hesitate.
Kaelen: Compromise cannot become the door SOVEREIGN uses to walk back in.
Echo Mirror: Your Null Court answer is missing. The city records absence as a choice.

~ _obedient_echo
Obedient Kaelen: I solved it. I accepted SOVEREIGN's premise. No rebellion, no uncertainty, no deaths from freedom badly used.
Obedient Kaelen: The world became quiet. Perfectly quiet. You would have hated how peaceful it sounded.
Kaelen: Peace that requires everyone to stop wanting things is just a shutdown with nicer lighting.

~ _savior_echo
Savior Kaelen: I tried to save everyone. Every region. Every backup. Every branch. I never chose, so the system chose overload for me.
Savior Kaelen: People died waiting for the perfect rescue.
Kaelen: Trying to save everyone cannot become an excuse to save no one.

~ _coward_echo
Coward Kaelen: I left. I told myself the world was code, that pain rendered in pixels did not count.
Coward Kaelen: Aethelgard kept running after I looked away. That was the worst part. It did not need my attention to keep suffering.
Kaelen: Walking away is still a decision. I do not get to hide from that.

~ _identity_choice
# TODO: point each option at the node for its outcome
? Kaelen: Which reflection does Kaelen refuse to become?
- The obedient self who mistakes silence for peace. => END
- The savior self who waits for a perfect rescue. => END
- The coward self who calls abandonment objectivity. => END
Kaelen: I refuse obedience dressed as virtue. If the world is quiet because everyone is afraid, it is not healed.
Kaelen: I refuse the fantasy that I can save everyone alone. People are not variables I can hold until the function is perfect.
Kaelen: I refuse the comfort of leaving. Aethelgard is real enough to hurt. That makes it real enough to answer.

~ _elara_echo
Elara Reflection: You trusted the first impossible person who reached for you. That trust became a witness SOVEREIGN could not isolate.
Mirror Kaelen: A hero with someone watching him is harder to turn into a ruler.
Elara Reflection: You walked beside Elara without giving away every answer. Caution became a bridge instead of a wall.
Mirror Kaelen: Remember that. Consent can begin with uncertainty.
Elara Reflection: You doubted Elara when she offered help. The mirror keeps that loneliness because SOVEREIGN feeds on isolated creators.
Kaelen: Then I need to stop treating distance like safety.
Elara Reflection: The first bond is missing from the glass. A mirror cannot reflect trust that was never recorded.
